 "about": "Exact polynomial ingredients of the variable-population-size Kingman class for sample sizes n = 4, 5, 6, as used by the deciders of popcorn.foldgate (foldgate_engine.py; register EXACT; every coefficient is an exact rational written num/den). For each n: 'm2_diag' maps the stored symmetric coordinate 'i,j' (1 <= i <= j <= n-1) to {exponent: coefficient} of the unnormalized component second moment m2_ij(t) = E[N_i N_j](g), t = e^{-g} in [0,1], of the single-atom limit history at level t (a polynomial in t whose exponents are binomial numbers C(k,2)); 'twotime_kernel' maps 'i,j' to {'es,eu': coefficient} of the symmetrized two-time block-count kernel Csym_ij(s,u) = E-sym[N_i(g_s) N_j(g_{su})] on the chart x = s, y = s*u, (s,u) in [0,1]^2, whose diagonal u = 1 is m2_ij(s). Produced by the exact two-site moment engine (lumped Kingman partition chain, exact spectral decomposition of the pure-death block-count semigroup); foldgate.load_ingredients() reads this file and foldgate.component_q() / kernel_sympy() / m2_sympy() turn it into decider inputs.",
